      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Epidural gas in the patient with sciatica can sometimes provide a clue that there is a surgically treatable lesion. Our patient had the sudden onset of sciatica at night, which was relieved by walking. An intraspinal synovial cyst was associated with epidural gas."},
